ause file collissions.  Explicitly add DEPEND on opengles-headers in the following packages that need the GLES headers at compile time: deqp, drm-tests, eglinfo, waffle.  BUG=chromium:656786 TEST=confirm no file collission when emerging opengles-headers  Change-Id: I5a7d3d6e1365e93540a1d3332929f0df41d50ae6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/400846 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="400846" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/46/400846/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I133e175fec2193fcc0d85861204c8e64f52521b8" commit="96484491786d73137afadf33e6ba4e85a89adef8" commit_message="drm-tests: Add support for EXT_image_flush_external_extension  The null_platform_test needs to call EGLImageFlushExternalEXT before every page flip if this extension is supported by the driver.  BUG=chromium:656786 CQ-DEPEND=CL:400846 TEST=run test on nyan_big  Change-Id: I133e175fec2193fcc0d85861204c8e64f52521b8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399958 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="399958" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" ref="refs/changes/58/399958/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If7ed10d8aedfb5e74946a6baab5c5a46c5cfa5a4" commit="917ad8aa6492c4b8d802a5c55708e1aa2822fe19" commit_message="factory_install_service: Apply TTY_CONSOLE settings.  For headless devices, they may come (especially by buildbot) with a default TTY_CONSOLE setting while /dev/console is empty.  That configuration also prevents kernel messages dumped on console.  To support this configuration we should look at TTY_CONSOLE (from make.conf) when /dev/console is empty.  Note factory_installer.conf is also reduced to prevent extra shell execution.  BUG=chromium:443972 TEST=Boots on headless device without adding --enable_serial and still seeing      right messages.  Change-Id: If7ed10d8aedfb5e74946a6baab5c5a46c5cfa5a4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/255347 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="255347" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory_installer" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory_installer" ref="refs/changes/47/255347/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I34c22c1f43d09bed4b0527d54438fb3079598128" commit="30dfddba6502b657becea22a8ae6648aae16ef2a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: fix wifi_diag accessing invalid skb memory  If RX_H handler returns RX_QUEUED, the rx-&gt;skb could be NULL or obsoleted value. Accessing rx-&gt;skb causes kernel panic. In this issue, the crash occurs after ieee80211_rx_h_defragment() where the rx-&gt;skb is set to NULL and handler returns RX_QUEUED.  BUG=b:32278492 TEST=Tested on Gale. Run iperf uplink and downlink traffic and      system is stable. Run and passed Jetstream sanity autotest.  Change-Id: I34c22c1f43d09bed4b0527d54438fb3079598128 Signed-off-by: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/401099 Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="401099" owne